I changed the trigger to enqueue a single batch `CaseSurveyJob` instead of one job per case. This is necessary because Apex enforces a limit of 50 queueable jobs per transaction; closing 200 cases in a single transaction would otherwise throw a `LimitException`. The queueable still processes each case individually and catches exceptions per case, so one failure does not prevent the rest.

